    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.splitjoin\n\n### Description\n\nNix lists are a little unique in that they don't use comma separators, just spaces, e.g:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: {\r\n  home.packages = with pkgs; [ cachix xclip signal-desktop qbittorrent ];\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.1 Build type: Release LuaJIT 2.1.0-beta3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In a Nix file with contents like so:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: {\r\n  home.packages = with pkgs; [ cachix xclip signal-desktop qbittorrent ];\r\n}\r\n```\r\n2. Try to split the list onto multiple lines with `mini.splitjoin`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe resulting code should be this:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: {\r\n  home.packages = with pkgs; [\r\n    cachix\r\n    xclip\r\n    signal-desktop\r\n    qbittorrent\r\n  ];\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe actual resulting code looks like this:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: {\r\n  home.packages = with pkgs; [\r\n    cachix xclip signal-desktop qbittorrent\r\n  ];\r\n}\r\n```",
