        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski this seems to break splitjoin for Nix attribute sets 🙁 🤔 \r\n\r\ne.g. if I have this, where `|` before `programs` represents my cursor position:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: { |programs.librewolf = { enable = true; }; }\r\n```\r\n\r\nit turns into this:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ pkgs, ... }: {\r\n  p\r\n  rograms.librewolf\r\n  =\r\n  { enable = true; };\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny way to fix that with a treesitter query or something? The default behavior of `mini.splitjoin` works for Nix attribute sets but not Nix lists.",
