        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Any way to fix that with a treesitter query or something? The default behavior of `mini.splitjoin` works for Nix attribute sets but not Nix lists.\r\n\r\nI don't think so. 'mini.splitjoin' is designed to have only one pattern to detect separator. In your original case it was space. It is possible to use `separator = '[ ;]'` but this won't work properly.\r\n\r\nIt is also designed to only work with Lua patterns, no tree-sitter integration is possible. If you want something more complex, there is [Wansmer/treesj](https://github.com/Wansmer/treesj) or [CKolkey/ts-node-action](https://github.com/CKolkey/ts-node-action).",
            "created_at": "2023-06-29T14:27:35Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/386#issuecomment-1613280252",
